        "original_id": "1c2c9088-2c3b-5f97-ab5f-ead03b9521fa",
        "text": "This chunk is about:\n- Places: Rhodesia, Northern Rhodesia, Southern Rhodesia, Zambia, Zimbabwe, Zambezi\n- Organizations: British South Africa Company, British government\n- Concepts: protectorates, colonial administration\n\nFacts:\n- The territory north of the Zambezi was officially designated Northern Rhodesia by the British South Africa Company.\n- In 1924, Northern Rhodesia began to be administered by the British government as a protectorate under conditions similar to other British-administered protectorates.\n- In 1924, the special provisions that had applied when Northern Rhodesia was administered by the British South Africa Company were terminated.\n- The territory south of the Zambezi was dubbed Southern Rhodesia by the British South Africa Company.\n- Northern Rhodesia has been Zambia since 1964.\n- Southern Rhodesia became Zimbabwe in 1980.",
        "type": "TextSummary"
      },
      {
        "id": 1,
        "original_id": "2cbc9145-bca3-56cc-926a-b86479c74996",
        "text": "Page: Rhodesia (region). Sentence: The territory to the north of the Zambezi was officially designated Northern Rhodesia by the Company, and has been Zambia since 1964; that to the south, which the Company dubbed Southern Rhodesia, became Zimbabwe in 1980.\nPage: Northern Rhodesia. Sentence: From 1924 it was administered by the British government as a protectorate under similar conditions to other British-administered protectorates, and the special provisions required when it was administered by BSAC were terminated.",
